  "targets": [
    {
      "order": 1,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0037",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s02-p057-01140-s005",
      "sentenceText": "Allport and Odbert also distinguished personality from the moral, evaluative concept of “character.”",
      "sentenceSha256": "921ceb745f82ff14e357d792ee1c422cd039278a0c81f1afb433ee72f0bb55bd",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s02-p057-01140-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-025",
      "parentFingerprint": "c915e0dcfd48419ada307f3b48d4daaacdcb78b2f7925fc33859c184a36aec81",
      "passageSha256": "ac951281c8a927babe1af541085b96f0d0c3b98865ab1d17a3a90843077b34d3",
      "pdfPages": [
        57
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 2,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0038",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s02-p057-01140-s007",
      "sentenceText": "So they removed all the character-evaluative terms, such as “excellent,” “acceptable,” and “insignificant.”",
      "sentenceSha256": "a2ed8e957acf80fa45608dc2d05097967cc1606657b83af25808685e82212ed6",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s02-p057-01140-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-025",
      "parentFingerprint": "c915e0dcfd48419ada307f3b48d4daaacdcb78b2f7925fc33859c184a36aec81",
      "passageSha256": "ac951281c8a927babe1af541085b96f0d0c3b98865ab1d17a3a90843077b34d3",
      "pdfPages": [
        57
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 3,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0039",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s02-p057-01140-s008",
      "sentenceText": "Allport and Odbert ended up with 4,504 “pure” personality trait words in English.",
      "sentenceSha256": "a0cadb0335f54515be55c2c348e3e3a051d653735f190d1ea7f9f0f478c984fb",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s02-p057-01140-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-025",
      "parentFingerprint": "c915e0dcfd48419ada307f3b48d4daaacdcb78b2f7925fc33859c184a36aec81",
      "passageSha256": "ac951281c8a927babe1af541085b96f0d0c3b98865ab1d17a3a90843077b34d3",
      "pdfPages": [
        57
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 4,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0040",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s02-p057-04260-s001",
      "sentenceText": "But why rely on words to illuminate an inner quality?",
      "sentenceSha256": "59b321de7559be3b4be79e5aff3fe6c1822d02acb7a00e6ccee6b8ebcb3b4a99",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s02-p057-04260-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-027",
      "parentFingerprint": "38430f3babd070a439f8f4926e91f557358a1cf9fa0ef29c94dc1af040c82a0c",
      "passageSha256": "aa37e174f13ea942797bf39073155befd8168876964d0c208748c4ffcaf8731c",
      "pdfPages": [
        57
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 5,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0041",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s02-p057-04260-s002",
      "sentenceText": "Allport and Odbert argued, “If many human beings were not in fact egotistic, aggressive, or timid, the epithets would not have found a permanent place in language.",
      "sentenceSha256": "12abec230473290fe267f7d7ec613a1c26079968549f23378bed1c18ab1c0996",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s02-p057-04260-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-027",
      "parentFingerprint": "38430f3babd070a439f8f4926e91f557358a1cf9fa0ef29c94dc1af040c82a0c",
      "passageSha256": "aa37e174f13ea942797bf39073155befd8168876964d0c208748c4ffcaf8731c",
      "pdfPages": [
        57
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 6,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0042",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s02-p057-05235-s002",
      "sentenceText": "For instance, the pure personality traits list included both “adventurous” and “venturous.”",
      "sentenceSha256": "02e3f9a35186ffc97abbfbc4f1ecd5879cfc00e6a2088165f4cac95ec6038724",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s02-p057-05235-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-028",
      "parentFingerprint": "970aa47ea17c2811f93c40e15f9e9c27ecf91317aecd0e407546c452baf14200",
      "passageSha256": "6b25ad2c9602eb9499a88fef5710d2da3b0f797229f8914131436c62a52ff9fc",
      "pdfPages": [
        57
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 7,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0043",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s02-p057-05235-s006",
      "sentenceText": "(Indeed, these words are not very useful.)",
      "sentenceSha256": "7fad0a240544543b43e06f7cc3b3da38ca416e5999be236ae98df93f9b6e05be",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s02-p057-05235-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-029",
      "parentFingerprint": "f23273e93bf409a6a30fdbfe80ff33b23b22ef38f2f2b588e7e752a9b3f12583",
      "passageSha256": "0af8cd38d87c3b8c044d95d390a4b2104cedb12a384fa755cfe60a4231934802",
      "pdfPages": [
        57
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 8,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0044",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s02-p057-05235-s008",
      "sentenceText": "(Probably true.)",
      "sentenceSha256": "1f6dce2e220272c4a9be39718673f3266f6b759ecfcf4a6cef707ef47f17d78f",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s02-p057-05235-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-029",
      "parentFingerprint": "f23273e93bf409a6a30fdbfe80ff33b23b22ef38f2f2b588e7e752a9b3f12583",
      "passageSha256": "0af8cd38d87c3b8c044d95d390a4b2104cedb12a384fa755cfe60a4231934802",
      "pdfPages": [
        57
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 9,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0045",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s02-p058-00750-s002",
      "sentenceText": "For example, Lew Goldberg had 187 college students rate themselves on 1,710 terms: “How jolly are you in general?",
      "sentenceSha256": "8086885a8743919c2b05b1661361d62f5daa0b66ca365717f24e1884def773ed",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s02-p058-00750-r005-005",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-032",
      "parentFingerprint": "c94269465bcd8fae1449fba73596e05fbfe6131ef8a0e1890465fb3faefb3c2e",
      "passageSha256": "f9d8ae22b039f6243e6da2ce6560102da3fc0079700ebf6e769cadc8bf32896e",
      "pdfPages": [
        58
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 10,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0046",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s02-p058-00750-s003",
      "sentenceText": "How reserved are you in general?",
      "sentenceSha256": "323bb86f5a1701ecb97b1c9fb803c1cd6a51e2c86f0b299f695018d04371dacb",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s02-p058-00750-r005-005",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-032",
      "parentFingerprint": "c94269465bcd8fae1449fba73596e05fbfe6131ef8a0e1890465fb3faefb3c2e",
      "passageSha256": "f9d8ae22b039f6243e6da2ce6560102da3fc0079700ebf6e769cadc8bf32896e",
      "pdfPages": [
        58
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 11,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0047",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s02-p058-00750-s004",
      "sentenceText": "How sadistic are you in general?”",
      "sentenceSha256": "5a19e079f2df5c0f2564886335ae7b39d154f7c85b73d0ee9fe6bc42b11d4e68",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s02-p058-00750-r005-005",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-032",
      "parentFingerprint": "c94269465bcd8fae1449fba73596e05fbfe6131ef8a0e1890465fb3faefb3c2e",
      "passageSha256": "f9d8ae22b039f6243e6da2ce6560102da3fc0079700ebf6e769cadc8bf32896e",
      "pdfPages": [
        58
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 12,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0048",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s02-p058-01920-s001",
      "sentenceText": "Goldberg’s study and others like it found that many personality traits cluster neatly into the following five factors: extraversion (e.g., jolly, talkative, sociable, active), neuroticism (e.g., touchy, fearful, self-critical), conscientiousness (e.g., persistent, tidy, dependable), agreeableness (e.g., generous, kind, trustful), and openness to experience (e.g., literary, insightful, perceptive).",
      "sentenceSha256": "11f61ea31ca5bd5b941a515205c79a4dd1c75264891d41ce1a1213347d8dc1f9",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s02-p058-01920-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-033",
      "parentFingerprint": "7e4e4fb093b2bbb1b534dcc382b5c40a3928a93f9cf6ea10df7872881d811b0f",
      "passageSha256": "6d21e311b673ac8e0bd2c7371096e8f4928f8a46ad326db9f0c46ac177fe9cf1",
      "pdfPages": [
        58
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 13,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0049",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s02-p058-01920-s002",
      "sentenceText": "In a sense, personality psychologists created a map.",
      "sentenceSha256": "dd3a9eb17bda6fd7c7582f47469406f64ca94e63443805f750adacd54d9110fb",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s02-p058-01920-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-033",
      "parentFingerprint": "7e4e4fb093b2bbb1b534dcc382b5c40a3928a93f9cf6ea10df7872881d811b0f",
      "passageSha256": "6d21e311b673ac8e0bd2c7371096e8f4928f8a46ad326db9f0c46ac177fe9cf1",
      "pdfPages": [
        58
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 14,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0050",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s02-p058-01920-s003",
      "sentenceText": "Like cities and towns across the world, there are countless words descriptive of personality.",
      "sentenceSha256": "94422bd17a57c262ac9e9fd4e66fc337ff089e7a7f7e3e25bf3d067ef0ecb9a1",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s02-p058-01920-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-033",
      "parentFingerprint": "7e4e4fb093b2bbb1b534dcc382b5c40a3928a93f9cf6ea10df7872881d811b0f",
      "passageSha256": "6d21e311b673ac8e0bd2c7371096e8f4928f8a46ad326db9f0c46ac177fe9cf1",
      "pdfPages": [
        58
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 15,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0051",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s03-p058-04575-s001",
      "sentenceText": "The type of person who goes to a pro wrestling match on the weekend might be a very different kind of person than someone who avoids those kinds of activities.",
      "sentenceSha256": "581f2506bb749f467003b539db6e2976bd93ac0515552dcf5574873f156d8151",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s03-p058-04575-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-035",
      "parentFingerprint": "d5d94e4ad1b5747ee463c9745e1368bbba680246fbdaf09ae6ef01b385a18048",
      "passageSha256": "d7562bef24a1c55a1c9867986d31d7f2e38cf54983ae7c543fe861a7a44500a1",
      "pdfPages": [
        58
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 16,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0052",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s03-p058-04575-s002",
      "sentenceText": "The type of person who studies abroad could be very different from the type of person who doesn’t.",
      "sentenceSha256": "1fe552d59a132320dc5bd246b3a465bb2cb594c2bb5679a6f86006f3c4ae2741",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s03-p058-04575-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-035",
      "parentFingerprint": "d5d94e4ad1b5747ee463c9745e1368bbba680246fbdaf09ae6ef01b385a18048",
      "passageSha256": "d7562bef24a1c55a1c9867986d31d7f2e38cf54983ae7c543fe861a7a44500a1",
      "pdfPages": [
        58
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 17,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0053",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s03-p058-04575-s003",
      "sentenceText": "Are there distinct personality traits characteristic of the psychologically rich?",
      "sentenceSha256": "5659a1f0b6b4243af94b2f71e0f5b868ed91e31722281448a87d178e62eddf9c",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s03-p058-04575-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-035",
      "parentFingerprint": "d5d94e4ad1b5747ee463c9745e1368bbba680246fbdaf09ae6ef01b385a18048",
      "passageSha256": "d7562bef24a1c55a1c9867986d31d7f2e38cf54983ae7c543fe861a7a44500a1",
      "pdfPages": [
        58
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 18,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0054",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s03-p059-01725-s001",
      "sentenceText": "Two main personality predictors of a psychologically rich life were openness to experiences and extraversion (see Appendix 2 for all the correlations).",
      "sentenceSha256": "7163a32d166bae915b9cdf1a87d705f8f6482e9c23af4e76a237e6b753282c7d",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s03-p059-01725-r001-003",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-039",
      "parentFingerprint": "4faf96810fd95952acc2a59dc9abcb8b75027a9d90aa99c14d02d9a1a3cda521",
      "passageSha256": "6866f5f6c75349022e5f09be82b46ce1a64ca368ae1c4cad7a4de3bfaf97d3d6",
      "pdfPages": [
        59
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 19,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0055",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s03-p059-01725-s005",
      "sentenceText": "For now, let’s focus on the link between openness and psychological richness.",
      "sentenceSha256": "487866340ebfb925a7dcab9af65b474fa7f6bc21c0c6da84894b02c92a463a72",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s03-p059-01725-r004-005",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-040",
      "parentFingerprint": "1b4cfdf8df43c74da8b800e0b556d4bea69a566c471b512f2430e3f9b0080191",
      "passageSha256": "40edee59aacfe46c6e9946c3cb9ecc5117e859e22dcaca79ae1d254a1a3cc22b",
      "pdfPages": [
        59
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 20,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0056",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s03-p059-03870-s001",
      "sentenceText": "Why do people who are high in openness to experience tend to lead psychologically rich lives?",
      "sentenceSha256": "93f69a2eeb40c8c29b1baf183754b9a7f2e8e37957dd75f7f1628f605be37226",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s03-p059-03870-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-041",
      "parentFingerprint": "1cafd6d519cde8ccfe42765dd4edb03ffce7e2c509ff725aa591a801822eb586",
      "passageSha256": "2136275a8be61ab44001ab63e3e70b83367486a98d0b5d585770ea2be97ae9c4",
      "pdfPages": [
        59
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 21,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0057",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s03-p059-03870-s002",
      "sentenceText": "Open people are imaginative, curious, and interested in intellectual and artistic pursuits.",
      "sentenceSha256": "e037b1d97867763218710722ef1d76a42e2e2aee8753f5bf7318fd0417aa38ec",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s03-p059-03870-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-041",
      "parentFingerprint": "1cafd6d519cde8ccfe42765dd4edb03ffce7e2c509ff725aa591a801822eb586",
      "passageSha256": "2136275a8be61ab44001ab63e3e70b83367486a98d0b5d585770ea2be97ae9c4",
      "pdfPages": [
        59
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 22,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0058",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s03-p059-03870-s003",
      "sentenceText": "People low in openness are conventional and down-to-earth, preferring routine and less interested in intellectual or artistic pursuits.",
      "sentenceSha256": "3fb875e94304274ac0ca8f88ff89394113ed746db968201ce6980eca189f4b25",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s03-p059-03870-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-041",
      "parentFingerprint": "1cafd6d519cde8ccfe42765dd4edb03ffce7e2c509ff725aa591a801822eb586",
      "passageSha256": "2136275a8be61ab44001ab63e3e70b83367486a98d0b5d585770ea2be97ae9c4",
      "pdfPages": [
        59
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 23,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0059",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s03-p059-03870-s005",
      "sentenceText": "Interestingly, those who studied abroad became more open to experience over time than those who didn’t.",
      "sentenceSha256": "5da0270064863b17b6cb7ecb04917d415250c94791fd2db88178761baf3f2380",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s03-p059-03870-r005-007",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-042",
      "parentFingerprint": "dd433a7aeb365cf3bbaaa270c2f4f3c3c31b4d14bc3e0f5bc42fadbaa55e63ec",
      "passageSha256": "8c86a59f147c68b37083677f74ed6697c79cdb9e47441d640ad75933f3827bc7",
      "pdfPages": [
        59
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 24,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0060",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s03-p059-03870-s007",
      "sentenceText": "Your personality is not your destiny, though; the later chapters of this book are dedicated to strategies that everyone, no matter what your personality is, can implement to make your life more psychologically rich.",
      "sentenceSha256": "87b97c4ee4c8ca0c2f8ab5d4ea0615269d4ebca5e87fb4ac28a06d63cfb458c6",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s03-p059-03870-r005-007",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-042",
      "parentFingerprint": "dd433a7aeb365cf3bbaaa270c2f4f3c3c31b4d14bc3e0f5bc42fadbaa55e63ec",
      "passageSha256": "8c86a59f147c68b37083677f74ed6697c79cdb9e47441d640ad75933f3827bc7",
      "pdfPages": [
        59
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 25,
      "questionId": "qe-c06-0061",
      "sentenceId": "c06-s03-p059-06795-s002",
      "sentenceText": "Joy Ryan, the ninety-four-year-old national park enthusiast we met in Chapter 4, might have always been open to experience.",
      "sentenceSha256": "0fd1b2640310a9f63c1875e24600d4ed38e6597b8ee6285f979befb04aa362ae",
      "readingUnitId": "c06-s03-p059-06795-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c06-043",
      "parentFingerprint": "ac76bd277742c19caa2bf15ba82075970272cb28b1cab6bb41c5b0e3fff99716",
      "passageSha256": "f78c561f9bd6a7d3f99f314420d2c613a3b4e6fe7d670748d8b100ce7bb41d0d",
